# Mandatory self-review before completing work

Before declaring any code change complete, you MUST:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and review every rule against your changes
2. Specifically verify (including current MCP / testing rules in AGENTS.md):
   - **`mcp` is a module-level global** — assigned at import time outside any function; FastMCP CLI-importable
   - **OpenAPI docs unchanged** — pass loaded specs into `from_openapi` as-is; no copy/deep-copy/path rewrite
   - **One `httpx.AsyncClient` per OpenAPI mount** — `base_url` from that spec’s `servers[0].url`; close all in lifespan/`finally`
   - **No `BaseException`** — use `try`/`finally` for cleanup
   - **No mocking** — no monkeypatch/MockTransport/fake clients; prefer DI + real local HTTP
   - **Assert full objects** — never assert partial responses (single fields, lengths, filtered projections)
   - **No enumerated variables** — use lists, not `x1`, `x2`
   - **No `time.sleep`** — never add sleep calls anywhere
   - **No raw DB access in tests** — all database operations go through `PostgresInteractor` when DB exists
3. Only after confirming compliance with ALL rules, report the work as done

If any rule is violated, fix it before reporting completion. Do not rely on `just check-all` alone — it checks tooling (lint, types, coverage) but NOT AGENTS.md conventions.

When a code review runs, the reviewer must also read `AGENTS.md` first and enforce it (see `.cursor/rules/code-review-agents.mdc`).
